WEBVTT

00:01.320 --> 00:03.940
Remember well, boy.

00:04.440 --> 00:08.150
That is the emblem of the empire
you'll live in from now on.

00:08.370 --> 00:09.490
The emblem...?

00:09.930 --> 00:11.080
Yes.

00:12.270 --> 00:15.530
The version our father drew was quite simple.

00:20.250 --> 00:24.250
We personally redrew it upon
our ascension to the throne.

00:24.560 --> 00:26.130
Pretty cool, eh?

00:30.970 --> 00:32.210
That's...

00:32.210 --> 00:36.590
...the emblem of the fallen
empire from my old world.

00:37.410 --> 00:38.480
But how...?

00:39.580 --> 00:41.740
<b>An alarming development</b>

00:41.830 --> 00:43.200
<b>-Why was it revealed?</b>

00:42.790 --> 00:43.200
<b>-How?</b>

00:43.250 --> 00:43.830
<b>In Japan, the "Bug"</b>

00:43.830 --> 00:44.500
<b>burned more of our brethren.</b>

00:46.500 --> 00:48.080
<b>-Sharp-eared as always.</b>

00:46.960 --> 00:48.250
<b>-What matters is that the public has seen it.</b>

00:47.620 --> 00:48.380
<b>-This will be nearly impossible to hush up.</b>

00:48.250 --> 00:49.840
<b>-Hide it.</b>

00:49.040 --> 00:50.000
<b>-But weren't they disguised as petty gangsters?</b>

00:49.710 --> 00:50.340
<b>-The Bug.</b>

00:50.340 --> 00:53.960
<b>Hide it in a forest.</b>

00:50.540 --> 00:55.090
<b>Hide it in a crowd.</b>

00:50.750 --> 00:52.630
<b>Bury it by revealing unrelated truths.</b>

00:50.920 --> 00:55.590
<b>Don't be rash.</b>

00:51.130 --> 00:54.650
<b>Claim it's the logo of some
upstart cult.</b>

00:51.300 --> 00:54.970
<b>It's a trap.</b>

00:51.460 --> 00:52.130
<b>It's bait.</b>

00:51.630 --> 00:56.300
<b>It's a lure.</b>

00:51.800 --> 00:56.300
<b>No one will fall for it.</b>

00:51.960 --> 00:55.170
<b>But someone set the trap.</b>

00:52.130 --> 00:55.380
<b>That's the biggest problem.</b>

00:52.300 --> 00:55.670
<b>We don't want that emblem getting around.</b>

00:52.460 --> 00:55.590
<b>But it's a serious problem.</b>

00:52.630 --> 00:55.470
<b>The problem is that someone baited a
hook for us.</b>

00:52.800 --> 00:56.280
<b>Who?</b>

00:52.960 --> 00:55.450
<b>The Bug?</b>

00:53.110 --> 00:53.960
<b>No.</b>

00:53.800 --> 00:55.670
<b>Solitaire.</b>

00:53.970 --> 00:55.380
<b>The Phantom Solitaire.</b>

00:54.130 --> 00:55.590
<b>An insignificant criminal.</b>

00:54.300 --> 00:56.300
<b>Send.</b>

00:55.170 --> 00:55.670
<b>Bury.</b>

00:55.380 --> 00:56.300
<b>Slaughter.</b>

00:55.470 --> 00:56.300
<b>Kill.</b>

00:58.050 --> 00:59.550
<b>Make it swift and painless. Don't give them time to suffer.</b>

00:59.550 --> 01:01.060
<b>Sadism feels satisfying, but it reveals more than necessary.</b>

01:02.140 --> 01:04.960
<b>Like that time five years ago.</b>

02:38.030 --> 02:40.090
What the hell is going on?

02:40.090 --> 02:42.210
Is that the symbol you mentioned?

02:42.570 --> 02:45.070
I guess I don't need to hide it anymore.

02:50.340 --> 02:52.400
It looks slightly different.

02:51.850 --> 02:55.320
At least choose the brand of your [...] yourself.
Corruption is eating away from the top.
Don't trust anyone.
There's another garage on the west side of that place.
The signpost is inside.
The key is behind the mirror of I-383.

02:52.400 --> 02:54.430
And Polka Shinoyama drew this?

02:54.430 --> 02:55.320
Yeah.

02:55.800 --> 03:00.630
If Solitaire is behind this, he must
be mixed up with Hosorogi-san, too.

03:00.630 --> 03:03.870
Or maybe with the people
Hosorogi-san was after.

03:03.870 --> 03:08.040
Either way, we keep running into this symbol.

03:08.510 --> 03:11.970
And it's all five years after
Inspector Hosorogi disappeared.

03:12.290 --> 03:15.930
Shouldn't we assume that's
more than a coincidence?

03:15.930 --> 03:17.170
Good point.

03:17.530 --> 03:21.260
It's also possible that Solitaire
has me in his cross hairs.

03:21.850 --> 03:27.260
Like, what if he was watching when
Polka Shinoyama read my fortune?

03:27.580 --> 03:31.570
We can't rule anything out yet.
We need more info.

03:32.450 --> 03:35.230
Oh, there you are!
Tsubaki-chan, Tsubaki-chan!

03:35.530 --> 03:36.450
Yamada-san?

03:36.450 --> 03:40.150
They're asking for you, and it sounds urgent.

03:40.150 --> 03:43.070
Me? Wait, who's asking?

03:43.800 --> 03:46.260
The top. Metropolitan Police HQ.

03:46.910 --> 03:49.860
<i>The metropolitan government
and police have announced</i>

03:49.860 --> 03:53.170
<i>that no blimps are cleared
to fly in the impacted area.</i>

03:53.170 --> 03:57.650
<i>Government insiders consider this
unlikely to be an act of terrorism.</i>

03:54.240 --> 03:58.990
The web is probably better informed
than the news at this point.

03:57.650 --> 04:01.260
<i>It may be an event staged by an extreme
collective of foreign artists.</i>

03:58.990 --> 04:01.880
Still, this was a splurge, even for me.

04:02.220 --> 04:04.370
I can't believe I sprang for <i>blimps</i>!

04:07.510 --> 04:08.390
So?

04:08.620 --> 04:11.850
How much does the information I want cost?

04:13.230 --> 04:14.770
Three trillion yen.

04:17.280 --> 04:18.660
Excusez-moi?

04:20.210 --> 04:21.710
Three trillion yen.

04:21.710 --> 04:26.480
It would be a bit more, but
for you, sir, I'll round down.

04:26.480 --> 04:28.280
Wait just a minute.

04:29.330 --> 04:30.910
How is that reasonable?!

04:30.910 --> 04:34.710
You only charged me 30 million for
three minutes of signal jacking!

04:34.710 --> 04:37.060
As I informed you earlier, sir,

04:37.060 --> 04:41.680
we adjust our prices to our
customers' circumstances,

04:41.680 --> 04:46.220
by which we mean the contents of their lives.

04:46.220 --> 04:49.390
I don't understand. Why does
that make it three trillion?

04:49.390 --> 04:55.600
If you seriously devoted yourself to
earning money by any means possible,

04:55.840 --> 05:00.290
we estimate that you would acquire
six trillion yen over your lifetime.

05:00.620 --> 05:06.910
It's a simple calculation, but this symbol
is worth spending half your life for.

05:07.410 --> 05:10.320
But please, don't misunderstand me.

05:10.320 --> 05:12.450
This price is only for you.

05:12.450 --> 05:17.930
If another customer made this request,
we might charge only a few dozen yen.

05:19.930 --> 05:24.590
To them, you see, this symbol's true
meaning would be merely a tall tale.

05:24.820 --> 05:28.840
A way to pass time, only as
valuable as a gumball to chew.

05:29.110 --> 05:32.180
But you are different.

05:32.540 --> 05:37.200
We guarantee that knowledge of this
symbol will shape your destiny.

05:37.200 --> 05:41.650
You might call it a miracle drug
just for the Phantom Solitaire.

05:41.890 --> 05:46.170
If mishandled, it will
poison and destroy you.

05:46.170 --> 05:49.030
For this prescription,

05:49.250 --> 05:52.650
three billion yen hardly strikes
us as an unreasonable price.

05:52.990 --> 05:54.250
I see.

05:54.250 --> 05:58.110
Your predecessor trusted you, and so will I.

05:58.420 --> 06:00.390
But our negotiation ends here.

06:00.390 --> 06:02.210
A wise choice, sir.

06:02.560 --> 06:07.200
After that buildup, hearing the
answer from you would be a letdown!

06:07.200 --> 06:10.000
I'll find it out for myself!

06:10.000 --> 06:13.680
Although I will pay for your help.

06:14.580 --> 06:17.770
I'd like to fly several blimps.
How much will that cost?

06:18.980 --> 06:23.310
Oh-ho! A human rope to tether an ad balloon?

06:23.310 --> 06:24.320
Now <i>there's</i> an i—

06:31.990 --> 06:33.640
Um, did I hit him?

06:33.640 --> 06:36.750
You missed. Look and you'll see.

06:36.750 --> 06:37.960
<b>Better luck
next time</b>

06:37.170 --> 06:40.220
So, we failed the mission?

06:40.220 --> 06:42.880
Beats me, but I doubt we'll get paid.

06:40.770 --> 06:42.880
<b>Better luck next time</b>

06:43.160 --> 06:44.400
Ugh!

06:44.400 --> 06:47.840
Shibuya, Ikebukuro, and now this!
We never get any good jobs.

06:47.840 --> 06:52.110
Wanna hit up Shinjuku? I hear good
things about an intermediary there.

06:54.140 --> 07:58.410
<i>Solitaire Shot?! Live</i>

06:54.140 --> 07:58.410
<b><i>Be afraid! A mysterious cabal lurks in our midst!</i></b>

06:54.370 --> 06:57.500
<i>Fifty-eight minutes after my blimps took off...</i>

06:57.500 --> 07:01.020
<i>That's how long it took
someone to snipe my doll.</i>

07:01.020 --> 07:05.430
<i>I wonder how they figured out
that I was on top of that blimp.</i>

07:05.430 --> 07:09.980
<i>The only things high enough to look
down on it are police helicopters!</i>

07:09.980 --> 07:17.290
<i>So, an organization with snipers accessed
police information in under an hour.</i>

07:17.290 --> 07:20.470
<i>Now to throw down the
gauntlet to my audience.</i>

07:20.470 --> 07:24.700
<i>Someone was ready to shoot me the
moment I revealed this symbol.</i>

07:24.700 --> 07:30.010
<i>I sense a conspiracy, a secret society.
It's music to my ears.</i>

07:30.010 --> 07:33.210
<i>It means such a dangerous group truly exists!</i>

07:33.210 --> 07:38.260
<i>You must be dying to know about
this symbol. Well, so am I!</i>

07:38.260 --> 07:41.060
<i>Tell me anything you know about it,
who uses it, and where!</i>

07:41.060 --> 07:46.820
<i>I'll gift a few lucky
winners 300 million yen!</i>

07:46.820 --> 07:48.620
<i>Will I really pay, you ask?</i>

07:48.620 --> 07:52.770
<i>Anyone who's followed my career
should know the answer.</i>

07:52.770 --> 07:55.040
<i>I'll tell you how to contact me later!</i>

07:55.040 --> 07:56.410
<i>Until we meet again!</i>

07:56.410 --> 07:58.410
<i>Oh! I forgot my sign-off!</i>

07:58.410 --> 08:00.660
The live stream has ended.

08:01.930 --> 08:04.010
This has turned into a real mess.

08:04.010 --> 08:06.290
Yeah. What're you gonna do about it?

08:06.290 --> 08:10.670
Let's think this through.
What should we focus on first?

08:10.670 --> 08:12.560
Well, you know.

08:12.560 --> 08:14.090
I guess I do.

08:14.090 --> 08:17.470
Yeah. I'd like answers, too.

08:17.470 --> 08:19.720
About empires and reincarnation and stuff.

08:24.220 --> 08:27.650
You'll tell me, of course. Right, Polka?

08:29.020 --> 08:30.190
Yes.

08:33.490 --> 08:33.970
<b>THE</b>

08:33.970 --> 08:34.470
<b>CORPSE</b>

08:34.470 --> 08:34.950
<b>GOD</b>

08:37.970 --> 08:40.990
<b>The Corpse God</b>

08:38.700 --> 08:40.990
Previously on <i>The Corpse God</i>.

08:40.990 --> 08:44.960
Polka Shinoyama (Fake) is the
Corpse God, a reincarnation!

08:44.960 --> 08:54.300
<b>Byady#erig Empire</b>

08:44.960 --> 08:54.300
<b>YEAHHH
YEAHHH
WOOHOO</b>

08:45.360 --> 08:50.360
In his past life he was hired as a court
sorcerer by the Byady#erig Empire,

08:50.360 --> 08:54.300
a military nation with no particular
interest in world domination!

08:54.300 --> 08:59.680
<b>The heroic Shagrua!</b>

08:54.670 --> 08:56.500
A hundred years after the empire fell,

08:56.500 --> 09:00.970
the heroic Shagrua, the Calamity
Crusher, struck him down!

09:02.390 --> 09:04.610
But the Corpse God cast a spell!

09:05.600 --> 09:09.620
He was reborn in Shinjuku,
in the corpse of Polka Shinoyama!

09:10.550 --> 09:14.590
There, for the sake of a peaceful life,
he battles insecurities about his future!

09:11.590 --> 09:13.050
<i>I've gotta
get a job!</i>

09:13.300 --> 09:15.150
We can skip the rest!

09:15.280 --> 09:16.940
And there you have it.

09:16.940 --> 09:21.200
The real Polka-kun's soul is safe,
and I'll return his body before too long.

09:22.500 --> 09:25.070
You seriously expect her to buy that story?!

09:25.070 --> 09:28.070
I thought things would actually
be easier if she didn't.

09:28.070 --> 09:30.540
So you're not gonna tell me the truth, huh?!

09:30.540 --> 09:32.680
Well, see if I care! Harrumph!

09:33.450 --> 09:34.600
Interesting.

09:35.780 --> 09:37.010
I believe you.

09:37.010 --> 09:38.680
You do?!

09:38.000 --> 09:39.260
Wow.

09:39.510 --> 09:43.220
I could sort of tell that you aren't Polka.

09:43.520 --> 09:49.310
You stayed calm when that cop
grabbed you. That's not like him.

09:50.140 --> 09:52.360
Still, I'm pretty shaken,

09:52.650 --> 09:57.400
partly because I don't want
to believe Polka got murdered.

09:57.640 --> 10:02.050
I'll go shower and calm down
before I ask for more details.

10:02.500 --> 10:06.800
Oh, and don't worry. I won't tell Xiaoyu
when he gets back from shopping.

10:10.020 --> 10:12.710
I can't get a read on her.

10:12.710 --> 10:15.870
Do you think I could show
her the dancing skeletons?

10:15.870 --> 10:18.930
Well, I don't think she'll
go around telling people.

10:18.930 --> 10:21.680
If worse comes to worst,
could you wipe her memory with a spell?

10:22.210 --> 10:28.520
I can make a spirit in my service possess
someone and remove parts of their memory.

10:22.780 --> 10:33.250
<b>Soul</b>

10:28.520 --> 10:32.380
The spirit would serve as a scalpel to
amputate a piece of the person's soul,

10:29.210 --> 10:33.250
<b>Memory</b>

10:32.380 --> 10:36.440
and that would indirectly
affect their physical brain.

10:36.440 --> 10:41.910
It's a different school than Geldwood
brainwashing and forced-confession spells.

10:41.910 --> 10:43.970
Is it hard to do?

10:43.970 --> 10:46.040
To be honest, not really.

10:46.040 --> 10:49.290
But that was on humans in my world.

10:49.290 --> 10:52.730
If this world's humans are
different in the wrong ways,

10:52.730 --> 10:55.360
a slight mistake could leave
the target broken.

10:56.950 --> 10:58.880
I guess we'd better not risk it, then.

10:59.240 --> 11:02.050
Of course, if we knew someone was an enemy,

11:02.050 --> 11:05.470
cutting corners and destroying their
minds could make things easier.

11:07.930 --> 11:12.410
Don't tell me... you messed
with those goons' memories?

11:12.410 --> 11:14.230
I did hold back.

11:14.230 --> 11:16.570
They won't be <i>completely</i> broken.

11:17.130 --> 11:20.320
Man, sometimes you scare the crap out of me.

11:22.090 --> 11:23.070
What?

11:23.540 --> 11:26.790
I'm kind of happy that you said "sometimes."

11:28.110 --> 11:32.030
Well, unlike Misaki, I didn't
actually get killed, so—

11:32.030 --> 11:33.210
Hey, wait...

11:34.250 --> 11:35.150
Where's Misaki?!

11:37.360 --> 11:38.110
<i>See no shark</i>

11:44.060 --> 11:45.300
Do you need something?

11:45.300 --> 11:47.390
Let's chat.

11:48.290 --> 11:49.420
About what?

11:49.750 --> 11:51.990
Didn't that story make you wonder

11:53.360 --> 11:58.020
who killed Polka-kun?

11:59.600 --> 12:02.090
Or does that not bother you,

12:02.440 --> 12:04.630
because you already know?

12:05.740 --> 12:08.480
I'd rather talk about sharks.

12:09.130 --> 12:11.350
Come on. Don't change the subject.

12:12.190 --> 12:16.590
If I told you I killed Polka-kun,

12:17.200 --> 12:18.100
what would you do?

12:19.390 --> 12:23.840
Oh, okay. So that's it.

12:25.030 --> 12:28.180
You want someone to chew you out, right?

12:28.710 --> 12:31.930
I'm guessing Polka forgave you.

12:32.510 --> 12:34.610
He's a gentle kid.

12:34.610 --> 12:37.730
He'd watch a man-eating shark
get killed at the end of a movie

12:37.730 --> 12:42.330
and say he felt bad for the shark,
as well as the people it ate.

12:43.110 --> 12:46.390
I'm going to ask for the details
of what happened later,

12:46.390 --> 12:50.830
but I'd bet that Polka
forgave you for killing him.

12:51.370 --> 12:54.690
You still haven't made your
peace with that, have you?

12:55.210 --> 13:00.480
So you want me to lash out at you.
It'd be part of your atonement.

13:01.130 --> 13:05.430
You're sly, but I don't mind. I forgive you.

13:06.110 --> 13:07.890
I won't chew you out, though.

13:17.520 --> 13:21.060
You're sharp. I bet you'd
make a great detective.

13:22.670 --> 13:24.190
Aren't you scared?

13:24.190 --> 13:27.820
I'm the assassin who slit Polka-kun's throat.

13:28.700 --> 13:30.030
You don't scare me.

13:30.980 --> 13:31.910
Why not?

13:32.570 --> 13:35.160
No one who likes shark
movies is a bad person.

13:38.300 --> 13:39.880
Umm...

13:40.150 --> 13:45.080
It was only for a little while, but I liked
talking about shark stuff with you.

13:46.390 --> 13:50.700
A bad person could never chat
about sharks and shark movies!

13:50.700 --> 13:55.140
You may have slit my relative's throat,
but sharks will forgive you!

13:55.410 --> 14:01.610
<b><b>His relative had
more of a screw
loose than he'd
thought.</b></b>

13:56.910 --> 14:01.610
<b><b>Faced with that fact,
the soul of
Polka Shinoyama</b></b>

13:58.410 --> 14:01.610
<b><b>decided to
pretend he
hadn't heard
anything.</b></b>

13:59.870 --> 14:01.610
<b><b>Hear no shark!</b></b>

14:01.830 --> 14:06.320
Plus, you saved Kazuki and Shizuki.

14:06.320 --> 14:09.700
That's my second reason,
although it doesn't count for much.

14:15.280 --> 14:18.540
Really? That part's the afterthought?

14:19.210 --> 14:21.500
Oh, jeez.

14:21.830 --> 14:25.270
I don't even know what to say anymore.

14:27.830 --> 14:28.930
For now,

14:29.860 --> 14:31.850
say something about sharks.

14:33.220 --> 14:34.640
So you see,

14:34.640 --> 14:45.590
<i>Silky Smooth</i>

14:34.640 --> 14:45.590
<i>Soft and Springy</i>

14:34.960 --> 14:39.470
I tried to find out if Sayo-chan
paid for that hit on Polka-kun,

14:39.470 --> 14:41.270
but I screwed up!

14:41.270 --> 14:45.910
Still, I'm pretty sure she
had nothing to do with it.

14:45.910 --> 14:47.380
Yeah, yeah. Whatever.

14:47.380 --> 14:49.610
What's wrong with you? Are you stupid?

14:49.610 --> 14:54.660
The only thing you proved is that
she's out of her goddamn mind.

14:54.660 --> 14:59.140
How rude. I just don't care much
about anything except sharks.

14:59.140 --> 15:01.920
So I wouldn't hire someone to kill Polka.

15:01.920 --> 15:04.280
I don't get your logic.

15:04.280 --> 15:05.460
Isn't it obvious?!

15:05.460 --> 15:06.440
<i>GLARE</i>

15:05.460 --> 15:09.010
If I killed him, I'd turn
him into shark food! Duh!

15:09.010 --> 15:11.260
I wish that wasn't so convincing.

15:12.720 --> 15:15.010
Don't tell me you took that
plushie into the bath?

15:15.260 --> 15:17.310
Not into the water.

15:17.680 --> 15:21.230
But I did borrow your Sharkborg
without asking. Sorry.

15:21.230 --> 15:25.190
With family like this,
you must've had it rough.

15:25.190 --> 15:27.660
I've never met that little guy before,

15:27.660 --> 15:30.900
although I do aspire to
make all sharks my family.

15:31.850 --> 15:34.620
Wait, you mean you didn't know
when you took him in there?

15:35.090 --> 15:38.580
U-U-U-U-Un...

15:38.580 --> 15:39.430
<i>THUD</i>

15:38.580 --> 15:40.290
Unbelievable.

15:40.290 --> 15:44.310
Yeah, getting seen changing can't have
been fun, even if you had no idea.

15:42.520 --> 15:44.310
I didn't peek!

15:44.310 --> 15:46.370
That doesn't matter!

15:46.370 --> 15:47.190
It doesn't?

15:47.190 --> 15:49.770
How could one of my
relatives become a shark?!

15:47.190 --> 15:56.430
I didn't peek!

15:49.770 --> 15:54.300
I thought for sure two souls were
fighting for control of that body!

15:54.300 --> 15:56.430
Rozan-san said the same thing.

15:56.650 --> 15:57.690
All right, then!

15:57.690 --> 16:01.940
Polka can borrow my body, so sharkify me now!

16:01.940 --> 16:04.770
What?! Wh-Why?!

16:05.020 --> 16:06.290
Totally
lost

16:05.790 --> 16:07.770
Speak no shark

16:06.290 --> 16:07.770
<b>Polka's soul chose
to let sleeping
dogs lie.</b>

16:08.390 --> 16:12.060
Seriously, though.
What's our next move, Polka?

16:12.060 --> 16:15.740
This symbol is a big deal to you, right?

16:15.740 --> 16:18.290
I don't mind people showing it in public.

16:18.290 --> 16:22.210
But if someone is trying to
use this emblem for something,

16:22.460 --> 16:24.420
I need to meet them.

16:25.010 --> 16:28.340
To us, it's a precious memory.

16:28.690 --> 16:34.300
I can't sit by while someone defiles
it and still live in peace.

16:35.900 --> 16:37.220
Okay.

16:37.490 --> 16:43.050
We'd better find out if some shadowy
organization really does use it, then.

16:43.550 --> 16:46.560
I mean, Solitaire could just
have been making shit up.

16:46.560 --> 16:52.030
You mean, that Solitaire guy is another
sorcerer from Polka-kun's world?

16:52.250 --> 16:55.870
No. He wanted information about the emblem,

16:55.870 --> 16:59.740
so I don't think he could be from my world.

16:59.740 --> 17:03.500
Can't you check with an identification spell?

17:03.500 --> 17:05.080
What do you mean?

17:05.080 --> 17:10.120
You know, where you see his level,
class, and skills just by looking at him?

17:05.730 --> 17:09.730
<b>Title
Great Guy in Shinjuku
| LV 01 |
HP 001/001 |
MP 001/001 |
ATK 001 |
DEF 001 |
SPD 001 |
DEX 001 |
CHA 001</b>

17:06.730 --> 17:09.730
<b>Title:
Corpse God
| LV 99 |
HP 999/999 |
MP 999/999 |
ATK 999 |
DEF 999 |
SPD 999 |
DEX 999 |
CHA 999</b>

17:10.120 --> 17:14.890
Oh, you mean what you
do when I tell fortunes.

17:14.890 --> 17:15.720
Huh?

17:15.820 --> 17:17.700
<b>I cast a spell</b>

17:16.030 --> 17:18.480
I cast a spell on the customer's name!

17:17.700 --> 17:19.180
<b>on the customer's name!</b>

17:17.700 --> 17:19.180
<b>Polka Shinoyama</b>

17:18.480 --> 17:20.890
<b>Now their info's mine!</b>

17:20.890 --> 17:24.350
<b>(Security)
Ineffective on targets of a
higher level.</b>

17:21.150 --> 17:23.960
I was an identification wizard all along?

17:24.350 --> 17:30.360
Anyway, I spent years crafting my
secret art of resurrection on my own,

17:30.750 --> 17:33.660
so I don't know if anyone else has come here.

17:33.660 --> 17:37.530
But you summon these guys
from your world, right?

17:37.530 --> 17:40.370
Yes. I was surprised that it worked.

17:40.370 --> 17:42.580
I only summon their souls, though.

17:42.580 --> 17:47.080
The bones are temporary vessels
I happened to find nearby.

17:47.080 --> 17:50.790
Then, do you know any
ghosts who can talk more?

17:52.280 --> 17:54.260
I... do.

17:54.890 --> 18:00.100
But I set most of them free before the
Order's last subjugation unit arrived.

18:00.550 --> 18:04.210
Some of them kept their pacts with me anyway.

18:04.860 --> 18:09.770
But how can I face them after I got
declared a threat to the world?

18:10.220 --> 18:12.690
That's why I want to at
least save my memories.

18:12.970 --> 18:15.020
Okay, enough whining.

18:15.020 --> 18:18.470
Call them whenever you want,
and do it with a smile.

18:18.800 --> 18:22.720
If they get mad or hit you, just apologize.

18:23.650 --> 18:26.790
Do you think... they'd forgive me?

18:27.250 --> 18:32.210
They trusted you enough to make
a pact. Have some faith in them.

18:32.600 --> 18:34.020
Sayo-san...

18:34.840 --> 18:39.090
<i>I'm sorry I ever suspected you
of having Polka-kun killed.</i>

18:39.370 --> 18:43.950
And if all this necromancy is real,
there must be sharkomancy, too!

18:44.740 --> 18:46.940
That's what really matters now!

18:46.940 --> 18:50.980
What's wrong? Shark got your tongue?

18:50.980 --> 18:54.630
Well, some people in the ocean
controlled schools of fish...

18:50.980 --> 18:56.820
<b>Sorceresses of the Deep
The Grimrope Sisters</b>

18:54.630 --> 18:56.820
Did that really deserve a serious answer?

18:57.050 --> 19:01.340
Anyway, you're wondering what
to do about that symbol, right?

19:01.340 --> 19:02.860
Pick the right man for the job.

19:03.780 --> 19:08.090
Leave that stuff to identification
wizards like me.

19:08.090 --> 19:09.370
You like that title, huh?

19:10.220 --> 19:11.700
Now,

19:11.700 --> 19:16.250
let's take a hint from Solitaire
and start by checking out the cops.

19:17.420 --> 19:20.880
I can't reveal specifics yet, but I have my suspicions.

19:19.740 --> 19:20.880
Really?

19:20.880 --> 19:23.780
Still... I won't stop you now, but tread carefully.

19:23.530 --> 19:25.950
The police organization, or at least part of it,

19:26.080 --> 19:28.850
is more sinister than you know.

19:29.000 --> 19:31.810
Metropolitan Police Department

19:30.580 --> 19:33.170
Sorry to call you up so suddenly.

19:33.170 --> 19:36.890
Don't be. I'm glad you're here,
Senior Commissioner Habaki, sir.

19:37.370 --> 19:40.730
I never expected to come back
here after I was transferred out.

19:41.060 --> 19:44.840
I wish you'd played by the
book and climbed the ranks.

19:44.280 --> 19:47.240
<b>Superintendent General</b>

19:47.240 --> 19:50.110
The superintendent general
wears many faces.

19:50.110 --> 19:52.710
Don't let him take you in. Now, get going.

19:53.790 --> 19:54.670
Yes, sir.

19:58.880 --> 20:01.670
You're in charge of the Solitaire case?

20:01.670 --> 20:04.020
Tsubaki Iwanome-kun, isn't it?

20:04.020 --> 20:04.840
Yes, sir.

20:05.110 --> 20:09.660
You look more like a host
than a police officer.

20:10.040 --> 20:11.760
Of course, given your division,

20:11.760 --> 20:14.990
I'll accept piercings and
dyed hair as camouflage.

20:17.110 --> 20:18.980
Only one thing matters.

20:19.590 --> 20:23.570
Can you function as a cog in this machine?

20:24.200 --> 20:28.050
I hope our teeth mesh well.

20:25.720 --> 20:28.660
<b></b>Metropolitan Police Superintendent General
Jirotarou Takasu

20:28.660 --> 20:31.870
<b>Jirotarou Takasu</b>

20:29.050 --> 20:31.870
So, this is the superintendent general.

20:32.220 --> 20:36.250
I know looks aren't everything,
but his face gives me the creeps.

20:36.250 --> 20:37.370
He looks so cool!

20:37.370 --> 20:38.840
You think so?

20:38.840 --> 20:44.070
Hm? That Iwanome guy keeps looking
for info about Hosorogi-san.

20:48.300 --> 20:51.930
Are you telling me he used a police computer for that?

20:50.330 --> 20:51.930
Until a few years ago, anyway.

20:52.410 --> 20:56.850
He was never good with computers...

20:52.590 --> 20:56.850
Looks like it got him in trouble.
There's a record.

20:58.570 --> 21:00.820
A cog?

21:00.820 --> 21:02.400
I'm sure we'll mesh nicely,

21:02.900 --> 21:05.870
Superintendent General
Jiroutarou Takasu, sir.

21:06.640 --> 21:09.670
I'm good at fitting in.

21:09.980 --> 21:14.500
Unless... there's a pebble in the works.

21:14.500 --> 21:20.210
Would this "pebble" be
Inspector Miyabi Hosorogi?

21:21.190 --> 21:23.170
I'll take that as a yes.

21:23.820 --> 21:27.370
I don't approve of you calling
a superior officer a pebble.

21:27.370 --> 21:30.400
Even one who's currently missing.

21:31.380 --> 21:38.050
Is that all Hosorogi-kun meant to you?

21:42.410 --> 21:46.280
Very funny, sir. I didn't mean the inspector.

21:46.890 --> 21:52.990
I meant the rat in this huge building
who drove the inspector out.

21:55.230 --> 22:00.420
I expected you to reject my suggestion
in a rage, but you're surprisingly calm.

22:00.680 --> 22:05.380
Although, amusingly, the way you
comport yourself is anything but.

22:05.610 --> 22:11.480
I see. Your cog may send a
new sound through the system.

22:11.480 --> 22:14.900
But take care.

22:14.900 --> 22:22.820
If I find the sound of a cog discordant,
I crush it without hesitation.

22:23.410 --> 22:25.150
I'll remember that, sir.

22:25.150 --> 22:27.800
Oh, one more thing before we begin.

22:28.850 --> 22:32.310
My name is Jirotarou, not Jiroutarou.

22:31.180 --> 22:39.500
<b>Jiroutarou</b>

22:32.310 --> 22:36.830
Jiro, not Jirou. Mind you
keep that vowel short.

22:36.830 --> 22:38.970
I'll remember that, too, sir.

22:40.130 --> 22:43.460
Now, as for why I called you here today...

22:43.460 --> 22:48.930
The Phantom Solitaire investigation has
been reorganized after today's incident.

22:49.540 --> 22:54.540
Given your history with him, I want you
to play a key role on the local end.

22:55.390 --> 22:57.770
<b>Shinjuku Gyoen
Shinjuku Gate</b>

22:56.400 --> 22:57.770
So?

22:57.770 --> 23:00.560
Has there been any activity
around the police?

23:00.560 --> 23:05.060
<i>Yes. Several people have
attempted to hack the police.</i>

23:05.060 --> 23:08.890
<i>One of them seems to know
what they're looking for.</i>

23:09.240 --> 23:11.270
Oh? Fascinating.

23:11.270 --> 23:13.700
And do you know where they're
hacking from, Nanny?

23:13.700 --> 23:16.660
<b>Nanny Café Amaguri</b>

23:13.700 --> 23:16.660
<i>But of course, Young Master.</i>

23:20.070 --> 23:22.500
The source is Shinjuku.

23:22.500 --> 23:23.730
Well, now.

23:23.730 --> 23:28.200
The office of a fortune teller
who just registered his business.

23:29.250 --> 23:33.910
I simply must have him read my future.
